# K03 S5 (Codex K03-S5-DEFINITION-TAIL-20261007-03): s, absent, retains `sendMessage: exit(...)` as its body: the
# definition sends nothing (exit 4 if it did), s() sends it in source order, count() read then (3 ticks: exit 7; 81
# if s() sent nothing).  In a method.
int: ticks 0
fn: tick () int
    node\ticks: node\ticks + 1
    return: 2
end: tick
fn: count () int
    return: node\ticks + 4
end: count
fn: check () int
    s: sendMessage: exit(exit_code: count(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    tick()
    tick()
    tick()
    s()
    return: 81
end: check
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: check(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
